    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text>
&lt;h3&gt;Worked solution&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Equation A is
\[
y={@m1@}x+({@c1@}).
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Equation B is
\[
y={@m2@}x+({@c2@}).
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
After plotting both equations,
their graphs meet at
\[
({@xI@},{@yI@}).
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Therefore the graphical solution of
the simultaneous equations is
\[
[{@xI@},{@yI@}].
\]
&lt;/p&gt;
</text>
    </generalfeedback>
